      "worked": "The inner function requires $x\\ne0$. The outer function also requires a non-zero input, so $f(x)\\ne0$.\n\nFor $x\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x+1}{x}&\\ne0\\\\\nx+1&\\ne0\\\\\nx&\\ne-1.\n\\end{align*}$$\nBoth restrictions must hold. Therefore,\n$$\\operatorname{dom}(f\\circ f)=(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,0)\\cup(0,\\infty).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
